<rml>
<head>
	<title>Settings</title>
	<link type="text/template" href="../shell.rml"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="settings.rcss"/>
</head>
<!-- Settings (docs/DESIGN.md 7.3, 7.5, 14): game folder and player name,
     display options passed to the game, launch options, look and
     accessibility, language, privacy and updates. Every change is saved at
     once. Data: the "settings" model in src/xerces_launcher/views/settings.cpp. -->
<body template="shell" data-model="settings">
<div class="page settings-page">
	<div class="page-title">Settings</div>
	<div class="page-sub">Every change is saved the moment you make it.</div>

	<div class="jump">
		<button id="jump-game" class="jump-link" data-event-click="act('jump game')"><span class="jump-num">01</span><span>Game</span></button>
		<button id="jump-display" class="jump-link" data-event-click="act('jump display')"><span class="jump-num">02</span><span>Display</span></button>
		<button id="jump-launch" class="jump-link" data-event-click="act('jump launch')"><span class="jump-num">03</span><span>Launch</span></button>
		<button id="jump-look" class="jump-link" data-event-click="act('jump look')"><span class="jump-num">04</span><span>Look</span></button>
		<button id="jump-language" class="jump-link" data-event-click="act('jump language')"><span class="jump-num">05</span><span>Language</span></button>
		<button id="jump-privacy" class="jump-link" data-event-click="act('jump privacy')"><span class="jump-num">06</span><span>Privacy</span></button>
		<button id="jump-updates" class="jump-link" data-event-click="act('jump updates')"><span class="jump-num">07</span><span>Updates</span></button>
	</div>

	<!-- 01 Game -->
	<div class="set-section" id="section-game">
		<div class="set-head">
			<div class="set-num">01</div>
			<div class="set-title">Game</div>
			<div class="set-desc">Where Black Ops III is installed, and the name other players see.</div>
		</div>
		<div class="set-body">
			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Game folder</div>
					<div class="set-value" data-class-missing="!game_found">{{game_path}}</div>
					<div class="field-help">{{game_detail}}</div>
					<div class="tried" data-if="game_tried.size > 0"><div data-for="line : game_tried">{{line}}</div></div>
					<div class="toolbar set-actions">
						<button id="game-change" class="small-button default-focus" data-event-click="act('change folder')"><span>Change folder</span></button>
						<button id="game-detect" class="small-button" data-class-disabled="game_busy" data-event-click="act('detect')"><span>Detect again</span></button>
						<button id="game-open" class="small-button" data-if="game_found" data-event-click="act('open game')"><span>Open folder</span></button>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="status-mark" data-if="game_ok"><span class="tick"></span><span>Supported</span></div>
			</div>

			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Player name</div>
					<div class="field-help">Up to 16 plain characters. The game reads it from boiii_players\properties.json in the game folder each time it starts. Leave it empty to use your Steam name.</div>
					<div class="field-note">{{name_note}}</div>
				</div>
				<input id="player-name" type="text" class="text name-field" maxlength="24" data-value="name" data-attr-placeholder="name_placeholder" data-event-blur="commit('name')"/>
			</div>

			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Binds and asset pools</div>
					<div class="field-help">Custom key binds and the larger asset pools big mods need, in the game's own files.</div>
				</div>
				<button id="game-files" class="small-button" data-event-click="act('game files')"><span>Open</span></button>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<!-- 02 Display -->
	<div class="set-section" id="section-display">
		<div class="set-head">
			<div class="set-num">02</div>
			<div class="set-title">Display</div>
			<div class="set-desc">Passed to the game every time Xerces starts it. Game's setting leaves the game's own choice alone. Not yet tried in a running game.</div>
		</div>
		<div class="set-body">
			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Display mode</div>
					<div class="field-help">Adds -windowed or -borderless to the launch flags; the game applies them after loading its own config.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="choices">
					<button id="display-game" class="choice" data-class-on="display == 'game'" data-event-click="choose('display', 'game')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>Game's setting</span></button>
					<button id="display-windowed" class="choice" data-class-on="display == 'windowed'" data-event-click="choose('display', 'windowed')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>Windowed</span></button>
					<button id="display-borderless" class="choice" data-class-on="display == 'borderless'" data-event-click="choose('display', 'borderless')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>Borderless</span></button>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Flip-model presentation (experimental)</div>
					<div class="field-help">Frames reach the screen without the extra copy through the desktop. Borderless can then present the way fullscreen does, and with V-Sync off its frames may tear. -xerces-flip-model. Turn it off if the picture freezes, goes black or the game crashes. Safe mode always leaves it off.</div>
				</div>
				<button id="flip-model" class="toggle" data-class-on="flip_model" data-event-click="toggle('flip_model')"><span class="track"><span class="knob"></span></span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="flip_model">On</span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="!flip_model">Off</span></button>
			</div>

			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">FPS limit</div>
					<div class="field-help">com_maxfps, 0 to 1000; 0 means no limit. Type a number and press Enter, or use the slider. Empty: the game's setting.</div>
					<div class="field-note">{{fps_note}}</div>
				</div>
				<div class="field-control">
					<input id="fps-field" type="text" class="text mono-field number-field" maxlength="4" data-attr-placeholder="game_hint" data-value="fps" data-event-blur="commit('fps')"/>
					<input id="fps-slider" type="range" class="range" min="0" step="1" data-attr-max="fps_max" data-attr-value="fps_stop" data-event-change="slid('fps')"/>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Precise FPS limit (experimental)</div>
					<div class="field-help">-xerces-precise-limiter: frames start 1000 / limit ms apart (4.17 ms at 240) instead of on the game's whole milliseconds. Uses a short spin of about 0.3 ms a frame, sometimes up to 1.3 ms. No effect at 0 or under 20. Turn it off if the game stutters. Safe mode always leaves it off.</div>
				</div>
				<button id="precise-limiter" class="toggle" data-class-on="precise_limiter" data-event-click="toggle('precise_limiter')"><span class="track"><span class="knob"></span></span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="precise_limiter">On</span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="!precise_limiter">Off</span></button>
			</div>

			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Field of view</div>
					<div class="field-help">cg_fov_default, 65 to 120. The slider's left end is the game's setting.</div>
					<div class="field-note">{{fov_note}}</div>
				</div>
				<div class="field-control">
					<input id="fov-field" type="text" class="text mono-field number-field" maxlength="3" data-attr-placeholder="game_hint" data-value="fov" data-event-blur="commit('fov')"/>
					<input id="fov-slider" type="range" class="range" min="64" max="120" step="1" data-attr-value="fov_stop" data-event-change="slid('fov')"/>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">V-Sync</div>
					<div class="field-help">r_vsync: wait for the monitor before showing each frame.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="choices">
					<button id="vsync-game" class="choice" data-class-on="vsync == 'game'" data-event-click="choose('vsync', 'game')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>Game's setting</span></button>
					<button id="vsync-on" class="choice" data-class-on="vsync == 'on'" data-event-click="choose('vsync', 'on')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>On</span></button>
					<button id="vsync-off" class="choice" data-class-on="vsync == 'off'" data-event-click="choose('vsync', 'off')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>Off</span></button>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">FPS counter</div>
					<div class="field-help">com_drawFPS_PC: the game's own frame counter.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="choices">
					<button id="drawfps-game" class="choice" data-class-on="drawfps == 'game'" data-event-click="choose('drawfps', 'game')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>Game's setting</span></button>
					<button id="drawfps-on" class="choice" data-class-on="drawfps == 'on'" data-event-click="choose('drawfps', 'on')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>On</span></button>
					<button id="drawfps-off" class="choice" data-class-on="drawfps == 'off'" data-event-click="choose('drawfps', 'off')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>Off</span></button>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="field field-stack" data-if="others.size > 0">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Other game settings</div>
					<div class="field-help">Saved in Xerces' config by something else; they are passed to the game too.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="dvar-row" data-for="d : others">
					<span class="dvar-text">+set {{d.name}} {{d.value}}</span>
					<button class="small-button" data-attr-id="'dvar-' + d.name" data-event-click="remove_dvar(d.name)"><span>Remove</span></button>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<!-- 03 Launch -->
	<div class="set-section" id="section-launch">
		<div class="set-head">
			<div class="set-num">03</div>
			<div class="set-title">Launch</div>
			<div class="set-desc">How Xerces starts the game, from Home and from Servers.</div>
		</div>
		<div class="set-body">
			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Skip the intro video</div>
					<div class="field-help">-nointro: no logo video when the game starts. The game then saves its own Skip Intro switch on, so Off here stops passing the flag but does not turn that switch off: do that in the game's Quick Settings.</div>
					<div class="field-note" data-if="intro_note != ''">{{intro_note}}</div>
				</div>
				<button id="nointro" class="toggle" data-class-on="nointro" data-event-click="toggle('nointro')"><span class="track"><span class="knob"></span></span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="nointro">On</span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="!nointro">Off</span></button>
			</div>

			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Skip all cinematics</div>
					<div class="field-help">-nocinematics: no cinematics or videos at all, campaign and Zombies included. The game then saves its own Skip All Cinematics switch on, so Off here stops passing the flag but does not turn that switch off: do that in the game's Quick Settings.</div>
					<div class="field-note" data-if="cinematics_note != ''">{{cinematics_note}}</div>
				</div>
				<button id="nocinematics" class="toggle" data-class-on="nocinematics" data-event-click="toggle('nocinematics')"><span class="track"><span class="knob"></span></span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="nocinematics">On</span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="!nocinematics">Off</span></button>
			</div>

			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Larger zone memory (experimental)</div>
					<div class="field-help">Lets big custom maps load with heavy mods. Turn it off if the game crashes. -xerces-db-pool: the game's 2 GiB zone memory for maps and mods becomes 4 GiB. Safe mode always leaves it off.</div>
				</div>
				<button id="db-pool" class="toggle" data-class-on="db_pool" data-event-click="toggle('db_pool')"><span class="track"><span class="knob"></span></span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="db_pool">On</span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="!db_pool">Off</span></button>
			</div>

			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Close Xerces when the game starts</div>
					<div class="field-help">Off keeps Xerces open, so it can notice a crash and offer safe mode next time.</div>
				</div>
				<button id="close-on-launch" class="toggle" data-class-on="close_on_launch" data-event-click="toggle('close')"><span class="track"><span class="knob"></span></span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="close_on_launch">On</span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="!close_on_launch">Off</span></button>
			</div>

			<div class="field field-stack">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Extra launch flags</div>
					<div class="field-help">Each a '-' then letters, digits, '-' or '_', separated by spaces, for example -console. Press Enter to save. Display mode, Flip-model presentation, Precise FPS limit, Skip all cinematics and Larger zone memory show up here too.</div>
				</div>
				<input id="flags-field" type="text" class="text mono-field flags-field" maxlength="1000" data-attr-placeholder="flags_hint" data-value="flags" data-event-blur="commit('flags')"/>
				<div class="field-error" data-if="flags_error != ''">{{flags_error}}</div>
			</div>

			<div class="field field-stack">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">The game starts with</div>
					<div class="field-help">What Launch vanilla on Home passes today. Launch modded adds the plan and the mods.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="command" data-class-bad="command_bad">{{command}}</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<!-- 04 Look and accessibility -->
	<div class="set-section" id="section-look">
		<div class="set-head">
			<div class="set-num">04</div>
			<div class="set-title">Look and accessibility</div>
			<div class="set-desc">Applies at once.</div>
		</div>
		<div class="set-body">
			<div class="field field-stack">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Theme</div>
				</div>
				<div class="choices">
					<button id="theme-dark" class="choice" data-class-on="theme == 'dark'" data-event-click="choose('theme', 'dark')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>Dark</span></button>
					<button id="theme-light" class="choice" data-class-on="theme == 'light'" data-event-click="choose('theme', 'light')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>Light</span></button>
					<button id="theme-contrast" class="choice" data-class-on="theme == 'contrast'" data-event-click="choose('theme', 'contrast')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>High contrast</span></button>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="field field-stack">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">UI scale</div>
					<div class="field-help">How big everything in Xerces is drawn.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="choices">
					<button id="scale-0" class="choice" data-class-on="scale == 0" data-event-click="choose('scale', '0')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>Follow Windows</span></button>
					<button id="scale-75" class="choice" data-class-on="scale == 75" data-event-click="choose('scale', '75')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>75%</span></button>
					<button id="scale-100" class="choice" data-class-on="scale == 100" data-event-click="choose('scale', '100')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>100%</span></button>
					<button id="scale-125" class="choice" data-class-on="scale == 125" data-event-click="choose('scale', '125')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>125%</span></button>
					<button id="scale-150" class="choice" data-class-on="scale == 150" data-event-click="choose('scale', '150')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>150%</span></button>
					<button id="scale-175" class="choice" data-class-on="scale == 175" data-event-click="choose('scale', '175')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>175%</span></button>
					<button id="scale-200" class="choice" data-class-on="scale == 200" data-event-click="choose('scale', '200')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>200%</span></button>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Reduced motion</div>
					<div class="field-help">Nothing slides or fades.</div>
				</div>
				<button id="reduced-motion" class="toggle" data-class-on="reduced_motion" data-event-click="toggle('reduced')"><span class="track"><span class="knob"></span></span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="reduced_motion">On</span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="!reduced_motion">Off</span></button>
			</div>
			<div class="field-note look-note" data-if="look_note != ''">{{look_note}}</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<!-- 05 Language -->
	<div class="set-section" id="section-language">
		<div class="set-head">
			<div class="set-num">05</div>
			<div class="set-title">Language</div>
			<div class="set-desc">Takes effect when Xerces restarts.</div>
		</div>
		<div class="set-body">
			<div class="field field-stack">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Language</div>
					<div class="field-help">Pseudo makes every string longer and marks it, to find text that gets cut off.</div>
				</div>
				<div class="choices">
					<button id="lang-en" class="choice" data-class-on="language == 'en'" data-event-click="choose('language', 'en')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>English</span></button>
					<button id="lang-pseudo" class="choice" data-class-on="language == 'pseudo'" data-event-click="choose('language', 'pseudo')"><span class="mark-dot"></span><span>Pseudo (test truncation)</span></button>
				</div>
				<div class="field-note" data-if="language_note != ''">{{language_note}}</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<!-- 06 Privacy (D21, decided 2026-11-05; docs/CRASH_REPORTS.md) -->
	<div class="set-section" id="section-privacy">
		<div class="set-head">
			<div class="set-num">06</div>
			<div class="set-title">Privacy</div>
			<div class="set-desc">What leaves this PC: crash reports, while they are on.</div>
		</div>
		<div class="set-body">
			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Send crash reports</div>
					<div class="field-help">When the game crashes, Xerces sends a report to the Xerces server, where the developer studies it to fix the crash. Off: nothing is sent, and reports still waiting are removed.</div>
				</div>
				<button id="send-crash-reports" class="toggle" data-class-on="send_crash_reports" data-event-click="toggle('crash')"><span class="track"><span class="knob"></span></span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="send_crash_reports">On</span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="!send_crash_reports">Off</span></button>
			</div>
			<div class="statement">
				<p>A crash report holds the crash's code, the game mode, map and mods, the Xerces and game versions, this PC's Windows version, CPU, graphics card and driver, RAM and display, the last lines of the game's and Xerces' logs (without chat), and a small dump of the threads' stacks. Your user name, player names, folders and server addresses are removed; the rest of the stack memory is raw and can hold bits of what the game was doing. It is tied to a random id kept in your Xerces folder, never to your name or your hardware, and the server deletes it after 90 days.</p>
				<p>Never sent: usage data or analytics, your Steam id or game identity, full crash dumps, your settings, packs or files.</p>
				<p>Voice chat in the game reaches the other players. Xerces starts a new game profile on push-to-talk (talk key B unless you rebind it) and leaves a profile you already have as it is. Not yet checked in the game.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Delete my crash reports</div>
					<div class="field-help">Deletes every crash report this PC sent from the Xerces server.</div>
				</div>
				<button id="delete-crash-reports" class="small-button" data-class-disabled="crash_busy" data-event-click="act('delete crash reports')"><span>Delete</span></button>
			</div>
			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Report a crash yourself</div>
					<div class="field-help">With crash reports off, open an issue on GitHub (DeroXP/boiii-free) and attach what Diagnostics &gt; Copy report gives you.</div>
				</div>
				<button id="report-by-hand" class="small-button" data-event-click="act('report by hand')"><span>Open GitHub issues</span></button>
			</div>
			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">What Xerces keeps</div>
					<div class="set-value">{{home_path}}</div>
					<div class="field-help">Settings, logs and caches, all on this PC; crash reports wait in its crash folder until they are sent. Full crash dumps stay in the game client's minidumps folder (%LOCALAPPDATA%\boiii\minidumps).</div>
				</div>
				<button id="open-home" class="small-button" data-event-click="act('open home')"><span>Open folder</span></button>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<!-- 07 Updates -->
	<div class="set-section" id="section-updates">
		<div class="set-head">
			<div class="set-num">07</div>
			<div class="set-title">Updates</div>
			<div class="set-desc">{{version}}</div>
		</div>
		<div class="set-body">
			<div class="field">
				<div class="field-text">
					<div class="field-name">Check for updates</div>
					<div class="field-help">The update client is not built yet, so Xerces checks nothing today. This choice is kept for when it is.</div>
				</div>
				<button id="check-updates" class="toggle" data-class-on="check_updates" data-event-click="toggle('updates')"><span class="track"><span class="knob"></span></span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="check_updates">On</span><span class="toggle-state" data-if="!check_updates">Off</span></button>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>
</body>
</rml>
